    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score makes him our clear standout play. Facing a favorable matchup against Elder (4.33 xERA), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a 16% park factor boost and a strong platoon advantage that positions him to contribute heavily across our 5x5 categories. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** earns a premier spot at 72.67; his lead-off status against Young (4.58 xERA) combined with a 16% park bump and a strong 0.387 xwOBA makes him an essential engine for our run production today. We are also leaning on **Jacob Wilson** (70.28) and **Heliot Ramos** (68.01) to exploit their respective matchups, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically seeing an efficiency lift from wind conditions projected to carry the ball out.\n\nThe decision to bench **Kyle Tucker** (51.31) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Kyle Tucker** possesses elite upside, the combination of a high-difficulty opponent in McLean (3.43 xERA) and a drop to the #7 hole significantly suppressed his projected efficiency compared to our starters. Instead, we\u2019ve prioritized hitters like **Jackson Merrill** and **Dominic Smith**, whose platoon alignments against their respective opponents provide a safer floor for our daily caps. While **Jackson Merrill** is our lowest-ranked starter at 59.99, his potential to capitalize on P\u00e9rez\u2019s slower delivery to boost our stolen base count\u2014the scarcest category\u2014keeps him ahead of the bench options. We remain cautious of **Nasim Nunez** (61.57) due to his low batting order placement, but his defensive and speed profile against Bratt remains a viable piece of our strategy to keep our daily efficiency metrics optimized.",
